.th MAZE VI 9/27/75
.sh NAME
maze \*- draw a maze
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd /usr/games/maze
[length [width]]
.sh DESCRIPTION
Maze draws a maze of given size in a format suitable for the lineprinter.
A path through the maze is an alternatingly vertical and horizontal
line which does not pass through a non-blank character,
and which ends at the exit at the top left
and starts at the entrance somewhere else on the perimeter.
.ti+5
There is guaranteed to be exactly one non-backtracking path through
any maze (i.e. the author would like to see any counterexamples).
If the length or the width is omitted or has 
(in the program's humble opinion)
an implausible value,
a default value is substituted
(currently 31 in either case).
.sh AUTHOR
Tom Duff.
.sh BUGS
